cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReasonedOps in research, teaching, demos, or derived work, please cite this software."
title: "ReasonedOps"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cheng"
    given-names: "Gigi"
version: "1.1.1"
date-released: 2026-08-21
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gigichengnc/reasoned-ops"
url: "https://github.com/gigichengnc/reasoned-ops"
abstract: >-
  ReasonedOps is a reproducible evidence-aware service-operations research/software
  prototype organised around Operate, Audit, and Evaluate. It converts unstructured
  service requests into explainable routing recommendations, preserves human and
  machine decision history, records outcomes, and applies an evaluation applicability
  gate before downstream regression/ANCOVA or alternative-method recommendations.
  The evaluation layer can withhold unsupported department comparisons when overlap
  or identifiability is insufficient. Current quantitative evidence is synthetic or
  hand-authored development evidence and does not establish real-world service
  improvement, causal effects, private-data pilot approval, or production readiness.
keywords:
  - "service operations"
  - "human-in-the-loop"
  - "evidence-aware evaluation"
  - "ANCOVA"
  - "regression"
  - "offline policy evaluation"
  - "longitudinal analysis"
  - "data governance"
  - "responsible AI"
